<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">skulduggery</ansi> (skill)

Skulduggery is the rogue's skill. Each level makes these surer:

  Finding and disarming traps (<ansi fg="command">help trap</ansi>).
  Picking locks (<ansi fg="command">help picklock</ansi>).
  In a battle, striking an opening on its own: a rogue's first blow that
  lands on a downed, stunned, staggered, or exposed foe is a critical hit
  (<ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>).

A rogue companion uses skulduggery for your company as it levels up
(<ansi fg="command">help autoskill</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trap</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help picklock</ansi>.
